WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.900
JEN PERSON: This
week, we're talking

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:05.440
about moving from 2019
to 2020, accessing

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.690
VPC resources from
serverless code,

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.660
and where to run
your containers.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.990
I'm Jen Person.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:14.010
And welcome to "This Weekend
Cloud," where we serve you

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.930
the lowest-latency news.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.740
We're glad to be back in 2020.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.680
And we've got just the thing
to start this year off.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.540
We've assembled some
New Year's resolutions

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.000
to guide you toward
operating a faster, more

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.950
efficient cloud infrastructure.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.140
Check out these tips
to improve your skills

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.880
and your architecture.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.392
And of course, if you're not
ready to leave 2019 behind,

00:00:34.392 --> 00:00:36.850
we've also got a recap of some
of the biggest announcements

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.500
and stories from last year.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.410
From hybrid to databases
to machine learning,

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.990
a lot happened in cloud in 2019.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:45.760
So make sure to get
caught up on stories

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.800
you may have missed,
and let them inspire you

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.010
for the new year.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.560
If you've ever wanted to
access your private resources

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:55.500
from your serverless
app, look no further.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.930
Serverless VPC access
lets you do exactly

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:01.260
that, giving you an access
point that lets your App Engine

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.530
and Cloud Functions connect
to VMs and other resources

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.200
with just a few lines
of configuration.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.580
Support for Cloud
Run is coming soon.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.760
So don't let your VPC silo
your resources any longer.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.180
Did you know there's
three easy ways

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.180
to run your containers
in Google Cloud?

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.090
Alexis gives us the details
on how you can run containers

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.950
with your Google
Kubernetes Engine,

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.890
Cloud Run, and even
Compute Engine.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:29.420
Watch the video
for more details.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:33.247
And stay tuned for more episodes
of Google Cloud Essentials.

00:01:33.247 --> 00:01:35.330
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:37.820
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.330
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:41.010
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.780
We'll see you in the cloud.

